        "body": "Bumps [github.com/layer5io/meshkit](https://github.com/layer5io/meshkit) from 0.7.87 to 0.8.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/layer5io/meshkit/releases\">github.com/layer5io/meshkit's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>MeshKit v0.8.0</h2>\n<h2>What's New</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>go version upgrade <a href=\"https://github.com/weilirs\"><code>@​weilirs</code></a> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/629\">#629</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Contributors</h2>\n<p>Thank you to our contributors for making this release possible:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leecalcote\"><code>@​leecalcote</code></a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/weilirs\"><code>@​weilirs</code></a></p>\n<h2>MeshKit v0.7.90</h2>\n<h2>What's New</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add support for logging print statements from rego <a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/628\">#628</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Contributors</h2>\n<p>Thank you to our contributors for making this release possible:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a></p>\n<h2>MeshKit v0.7.89</h2>\n<h2>What's New</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Design Enrichment logic <a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/626\">#626</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Contributors</h2>\n<p>Thank you to our contributors for making this release possible:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a></p>\n<h2>MeshKit v0.7.88</h2>\n<h2>What's New</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>remove asset deduplication for component/model svgs <a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/625\">#625</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Contributors</h2>\n<p>Thank you to our contributors for making this release possible:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aabidsofi19\"><code>@​aabidsofi19</code></a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/0343f9e87f2010b8c2771cc5911e97dc3abe2a11\"><code>0343f9e</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/629\">#629</a> from weilirs/go-version-upgrade</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/1ef30f2ec37803429c8a8adfc544d9e3061b258d\"><code>1ef30f2</code></a> go version upgrade</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/a30e177e8169eb874c4af9b6d1fffab62199fdd9\"><code>a30e177</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/628\">#628</a> from aabidsofi19/rego-print</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/9f59a993e49326b5f913bf2d5391579435a224e2\"><code>9f59a99</code></a> remove wrong option</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/bc26d07b2e0bc4365eee2fedb6def313f6d8d6af\"><code>bc26d07</code></a> add control arg</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/1ae857ce0d29439403accdbd060e9228c86bc2b4\"><code>1ae857c</code></a> Add support for logging print statements from rego</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/4fc6b1d74261a48d2f9f2be43f2b0ca09f0728e0\"><code>4fc6b1d</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/layer5io/meshkit/issues/626\">#626</a> from aabidsofi19/design-orchestration</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/b34f5cb8c614aad29feaf7a2ebf37beb1fa02dcd\"><code>b34f5cb</code></a> annotate with version than name</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/f3e2d761aede505a21d12dbcdd3f36b41ec9bc97\"><code>f3e2d76</code></a> add logic for assign meshery specific labels and annotations</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/meshery/meshkit/commit/e717d52339cfdee0737b7fa85d765dbf6eb9de12\"><code>e717d52</code></a> add constants for meshery specific labels</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/layer5io/meshkit/compare/v0.7.87...v0.8.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=github.com/layer5io/meshkit&package-manager=go_modules&previous-version=0.7.87&new-version=0.8.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot merge` will merge this PR after your CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot squash and merge` will squash and merge this PR after your CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot cancel merge` will cancel a previously requested merge and block automerging\n- `@dependabot reopen` will reopen this PR if it is closed\n- `@dependabot close` will close this PR and stop Dependabot recreating it. You can achieve the same result by closing it manually\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>",
