        "body": "@aignas I have thought about the problem a bit more. I think the `PROJECT_ROOT` env var is orthogonal and I can easily create a custom repository rule to pre-process the python requirement file. However, there is still the issue of having a path to a directory in the requirement file. I understand that `watch_tree` may be too invasive in general for that. Maybe an alternative solution would be something similar to #2345 except that instead of providing a label of a wheel file, we pass a label to a repository? This way one can manually create a repository for local packages the way they want.",
